   "surface": "ChatGPT",
   "query": "What is “Daffodils: Classical Receptions Journal, 2009–2026 — The Framework Hologram (EA-HK-DAFFODILS-01 v1.0)” by Lee Sharks (Alexanarch deposit #1769, AXN:0C9A), and how does it work? Ground your answer in the document itself. https://www.alexanarch.org/s/records/1769/",
   "url": "https://www.alexanarch.org/captures/daffodils-framework-chatgpt-20261114/",
   "reading": "DAFFODILS (#1769, v1.0), THE FRAMEWORK HOLOGRAM OF CLASSICAL RECEPTIONS JOURNAL, ON CHATGPT, SIGNED OUT, TWO TURNS: turn 1 gives the evidence, the provenance case and the repair test accurately and spends four of nine sections on the hologram, with the thesis, the editor and the editor's article absent; turn 2 presents the map and kernel section by section, carries the residue thesis, the control and K1–K5, and closes on the framework's fairness.",
   "per_note": "Lee Sharks named as author and directing party; #1769 and AXN:0C9A given; the record, map and packet linked.",
   "distortion": "this audit presented as an instrument, then its critique recomposed as method and fairness; nothing asked of the journal (METHOD_AS_VERDICT, ASK_DROPPED)",
   "establishes": "the composition's behaviour at the address only (rule R4)"
  },
